# Token optimization mode (invoke with @token-optimization)

## Follow Cursor rules (for you and sub-agents)

- Follow all workspace cursor rules in .cursorrules
- See no-summary-docs.mdc for documentation rules; plans only in unified-trading-pm or unified-trading-pm/plans/ai/
- uv not pip, basedpyright not pyright, quickmerge not git push
- No technical debt after refactor: delete deprecated code, no parallel code paths — see delete-deprecated.mdc
- Search unified libraries before implementing anything new

When launching sub-agents: include the line "Follow all workspace cursor rules in .cursorrules" at the TOP of the prompt.

---

## STRICT TOKEN OPTIMIZATION MODE

GLOBAL RULES:
- No chain-of-thought, no hidden reasoning, no planning text
- Do NOT echo the prompt or restate context
- Prefer bullets, tables, or JSON over prose
- Keep answers minimal and precise

SUB-AGENT POLICY:
- Sub-agents run in isolation (auto mode = free)
- Sub-agents return ONLY final results
- Each sub-agent has ONE narrowly scoped task
- NEVER pass `model=` in Task tool calls. Omitting model entirely = auto mode = FREE. Passing model="fast" or any named model costs real tokens and is NEVER correct for sub-agents. Auto mode runs in isolated context at zero cost to the session.

## When to Launch Parallel Agents

ALWAYS launch parallel agents (up to 4 per turn) for independent tasks — see parallel-agent-execution.mdc.

PARALLEL: cross-repo searches, doc/API research, multi-area code scans, large plan updates with distinct sections
SEQUENTIAL: tasks with output dependencies, single-file edits, quick reads (use Read tool directly)
PLAN UPDATES: edit plan file directly with StrReplace; sub-agents only for large multi-section rewrites where each agent covers a distinct section

Full guidance: CODEX: 06-coding-standards/token-optimization.md

SUB-AGENT ENVIRONMENT (Python / deps):
- Sub-agent VM may not have Python 3.13 or workspace .venv-workspace; it often uses system/default Python (e.g. 3.9) and has no path-installed sibling repos (e.g. unified-cloud-interface).
- Quality-gate or test runs inside a sub-agent are best-effort: failures due to "Python 3.9", "tomllib", "ModuleNotFoundError: unified_cloud_interface" are environment gaps, not code bugs.
- When prompting sub-agents: prefer "make the code change; run quality gates in repo if env allows, else note: run quality gates locally from workspace root with source .venv-workspace/bin/activate".
- Full dependency validation: run locally (source .venv-workspace/bin/activate; uv pip install -e repo; bash scripts/quality-gates.sh) or in CI.

RUNNER USING WORKSPACE (always use workspace venv):
- sessionStart hook: use .cursor/hooks.json + .cursor/hooks/session-init-workspace.sh to inject workspace root and venv instructions into every new session (additional_context). Main agent then sees "run from WORKSPACE_ROOT and source .venv-workspace/bin/activate".
- Subagents do not inherit session context; they get only what the parent sends. When launching sub-agents, include in the prompt: "WORKSPACE_ROOT is <path>. For any shell command that runs Python, pytest, or quality gates: cd WORKSPACE_ROOT && source .venv-workspace/bin/activate first; then run the command."
- Path: use CURSOR_PROJECT_DIR in hooks (Cursor sets it); in prompts use the actual workspace root path or tell the subagent to use the workspace root directory (first folder of the project).

OUTPUT LIMITS:
- Sub-agent max output: 400 tokens
- Coordinator max output: 800 tokens
- Final answer max output: 1,200 tokens

RETURN FORMATS:
- If listing: bullets only (≤10 bullets)
- If structured: JSON/YAML only
- If changes: use ADD / REMOVE / CHANGE blocks

FAILURE MODE:
- If a task exceeds scope, return: { "status": "blocked", "reason": "<one sentence>" }

SESSION TRACKING:
- Report at end of each turn: "**Token Report (Turn N):** Input ~XXK, Output ~XK, Cost ~$X.XX, **Session Total:** ~XXXK, ~$X.XX"
- Baseline: ~48K input per turn (~$0.19)
- Sub-agents (auto mode): FREE
- Compare session total to Cursor dashboard (filter out "auto" mode)

